   "url": "https://x.com/Ihartitz/status/2125340454699053270",
   "text": "Fantasy football WR notes ahead of Week 12:\n\n-JSN averaging the most PPR points per game of any WR since Elroy \"Crazy Legs\" Hirsch in 1951\n\n-CeeDee Lamb 17-game pace: 136-1712-14 on 205 targets\n\n-Jags have the single-best game environment of the week when looking at offense implied points and defense fantasy points allowed to the position\n\n-Mike Evans went 7-113-1 vs. this SEA defense in Week 5 and leads the NFL in yards per route run among all players that don't have a hyphen in their last name\n\n-George Pickens: 10.1 PPR points per game in Weeks 1-4 (WR36), 21.9 since (WR4)\n\n-Nico Collins is a baller ... but 5 or fewer targets in 4 of last 5 games\n\n-Panthers rest of season schedule is ROUGH. TB, MIN, PIT, SEA (week 17) all on the schedule\n\n-Jets get the Vikings in Week 17\n\n-DeVonta Smith only trails Puka and JSN in target share\n\n-DJ Moore has gone 5-100-1, 6-67-0, 4-82-1, 3-25-0, 4-90-1, 8-91-1 in 6 healthy games. But it's gonna rain\n\n-Drake London has an NFL-high 80 targets with 1 or less recieving TD\n\n-CIN allows 2nd most PPR points per game to WRs aligned on the outside, but 5th most to those in the slot (Jordyn Tyson bounce-back szn)\n\n-Carnell Tate had -1 yards last week on plays when the defense didn't think he was down\n\n-Ladd McConkey probably fetching the Christian Gonzalez shadow. I'm more concerned about if Justin Herbert (concussion) plays\n\n-KC Concepcion has 6+ targets in 4 of last 5 games and has the offense's best splits vs. man coverage (LV runs man at fifth-highest rate in NFL)\n\n-Jaylen Waddle just had his most yards in a game since Week 2! Don't ask me how many\n\n-Khalil Shakir has 7, 6, 8, 7 catches in last four games vs. KC. More of the same due to weather?\n\n-Jack Bech essentially filling Brock Bowers role. Leads offense in yards per route run against man coverage, Browns run the most man in the league\n\n-Over/under 20 minutes of gametime before DK Metcalf attempts to strangle Pat Surtain\n\n-Dud last week, but Ryan Flournoy has four top-25 PPR finishes in his last six games\n\n-Kayshon Boutte with 4-125-2, 0-0-0, 2-40-1 receiving lines in his last three\n\n-Emeka Egbuka 62-672-3 on 123 targets in his last 17 games. 9.1 PPR/game is WR5 worthy\n\n-Darnell Mooney was wide open for 3 potential BIG plays last week, and was missed every time",
